{"name":"Boysenberry Shadow","hex":"#f1f3f9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boysenberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hybrid berry created from crossing blackberry, red raspberry, and loganberry.","A colour of the purple colour spectrum, based on the boysenberry's colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boysenberry"},{"term":"shadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark image projected onto a surface where light (or other radiation) is blocked by the shade of an object.","Relative darkness, especially as caused by the interruption of light; gloom; obscurity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unofficial, informal, unauthorized, but acting as though it were.","Having power or influence, but not widely known or recognized."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boysenberry","blocks":[{"text":"The boysenberry is a cross between the European raspberry, European blackberry, American dewberry, and loganberry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Boysenberries.jpg/330px-Boysenberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boysenberry","wikidata":"Q896083"},{"title":"Shadow","blocks":[{"text":"A shadow is a dark area on a surface where light from a light source is blocked by an object. In contrast, shade occupies the three-dimensional volume behind an object with light in front of it. The cross-section of a shadow is a two-dimensional silhouette, or a reverse projection of the object blocking the light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg/330px-The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow","wikidata":"Q160020"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://th